// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`immutable source > explains directory-first reverse engineering and scoped reads > directory inspection guide 1`] = `"For an imported directory, including reverse-engineering materials, start with directory and path "" (root). It lists immediate children with descendant file counts and byte sizes, without reading member contents. File extensions and text flags are hints, not verified formats. Enter only task-relevant subdirectories, then select relevant files for targeted text reads or binary identity and specialist analysis. Do not inspect every file or decompile every function merely because it was imported. directory accepts path (default root), offset and limit; list retains the flat manifest with offset and limit. read requires an exact path and accepts startLine (1-based), limit. search requires a literal query and accepts either an exact path or a directory subtree, offset and limit; omitting both searches all text files, so narrow the scope first. Paths belong to the immutable snapshot, never the live filesystem. Results include hashes, exclusions and continuation positions; uninspected files remain uninspected."`;
